          "date": "2026-11-25 16:19:15.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20791 efalnd: Refresh peer NI data from a connection probe",
        "message": "LU-20791 efalnd: Refresh peer NI data from a connection probe\n\nWhen a peer restarts, its connection manager QP changes. The cached\npeer NI data holding the peer's address and manager QP lives as long\nas any connection uses it, and a probe that created a new responder\nconnection reused it without updating it. Our reply went to the old\nQP, so the peer could not connect until all old connections were\ngone. A probe from a restarted peer that found a connection still\nbeing set up was answered with the peer's old epoch, which the peer\ndrops, and through the old address.\n\nUpdate the peer NI data from the probe when creating a responder\nconnection, and replace a connection still being set up whose peer\nrestarted, as is already done for an active one.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nChange-Id: I7d0ef7457331e87d340bd5fc009ef481ba4ce501\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
